@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: Environment Routing
	Testing the routing of specific tickets to various environments

Teardown:
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown users with the following userExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| User1 |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Organization1 |

Scenario: Production Environment Routing
	End users who create requests with any status containing the term production should have their tickets routed to the Production environment.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp_cloud   |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | Regular             |
	| Support Region   | US                  |
	| Support Language | English             | 
	| External ID      | Organization1       |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Portuguese                       |
	| Time Zone        | Brasilia                         | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with the following product, component, and system status values
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_1    | apio_architect                | production_completely_shutdown      |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_0    | application_display_templates | production_severely_impacted_inoperable     |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2 | authentication                | production_unstable_with_periodic_interruptions      |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_1 | caching_clustering            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities     |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_0 | calendar                      | production_fully_functional_with_observed_errors     |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the environment "production"

Scenario: Non Production Environment Routing
	End users who create requests with any status containing the term non-production should have their tickets routed to the Non-Production environment.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp_cloud   |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | Regular             |
	| Support Region   | US                  |
	| Support Language | English             | 
	| External ID      | Organization1       |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Portuguese                       |
	| Time Zone        | Brasilia                         | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with the following product, component, and system status values
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_1    | apio_architect                | non-production_completely_shutdown      |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_0    | application_display_templates | non-production_severely_impacted_inoperable     |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2 | authentication                | non-production_unstable_with_periodic_interruptions      |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_1 | caching_clustering            | non-production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities     |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_0 | calendar                      | non-production_fully_functional_with_observed_errors     |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the environment "non-production"